  "problem": "What was the exact rate of change of the stock's value at week $4?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\,$ thousand dollars per week.",
  "worked_solution": "The function ${g}^{\u2032}(x)$ models the rate of change of the value of the stock, applicable in the domain of $g(x).$\n\nThus, the rate of change of the value of the stock at $x=4$ weeks is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(4) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the stock price was $\\frac{1}{2}$ thousand dollars per week.",
